# Working notes stay local. Named here, and the cost of naming them is
# accepted: this file is the only exclusion a clone carries, and
# `.git/info/exclude` is not cloned -- so moving these there left every
# fresh checkout one `git add -A` away from committing them, which is a
# worse thing to publish than the names.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/.claude/
/docs/findings.md
/docs/audits.md

# The release workflow writes these into the workspace. Two of its
# steps already use mktemp for exactly this reason, with a comment
# saying a stray file is one `git add -A` from a commit; the third
# does not, and this is the cheap half of that repair.
/notes.md
/offline/
